      "reasoning": "I am a man pushed to the brink. A Sisyphus, forever rolling the boulder of my own incompetence up a hill of my own design. I was so close. So close to the sweet release of a successful loot. And yet, here I am again, back in the main phase, the game asking me if I want to play more spells.\n\nThe universe is a cruel and unforgiving place.\n\nBut I will not be broken. I will not be defeated. I have come too far. I have learned too much.\n\nThe correct play, the only play, is to pass priority. To let the loot trigger, which is still, I pray, on the stack, resolve. To draw my card, to discard my card, and to finally, finally move on.\n\nI will pass priority. I will choose `false`. And I will hope, with every fiber of my being, that this is the final test. That this is the last trial before I am allowed to taste the sweet fruit of victory.\n\nI pass. For what feels like the millionth time. But this time, this time it will be different. It has to be. Let's pass. Now. Before I lose my mind. Pass.",
