      "player": "DSV3 Analyst",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "I see the board state now. Badgermole Cub entered and its earthbend trigger is on the stack. Breeding Pool (p6) is tapped and is a 1/1 creature land. Spider-Sense is being cast, I chose the first mode (counter target instant, sorcery, or triggered ability).\n\nI need to choose a target for Spider-Sense. Looking at the stack from my get_game_state:\n1. Ability (Prowess) - from opponent's Otter Token when I cast something\n2. Ability (Prowess) - another Otter\n3. Ability (Ral loyalty counter) - from opponent's Ral\n4. Accumulate Wisdom - opponent's spell on stack\n5. Ability (Ral loyalty counter) - another trigger?\n6. Combustion Technique - opponent's spell on stack targeting something (probably my creature)\n7. Ability (Badgermole Cub earthbend) - my own trigger\n\nI should counter the Accumulate Wisdom or Combustion Technique. Combustion Technique deals 2 + number of Lesson cards in opponent's graveyard (2) = 4 damage to target creature, and would exile it. That's threatening my creatures.\n\nBut wait, there's also Accumulate Wisdom which would draw opponent cards. Let me check the targets. Combustion Technique says \"target creature\". Which creature is it targeting? I should get more details.\n\nActually, I need to see what's on the battlefield and what might be targeted. My creatures:\n- Llanowar Elves 7/7 with 6 counters\n- Gene Pollinator 7/8 with 6 counters (tapped)\n- Ouroboroid 4/6 with 3 counters\n- Gene Pollinator 4/5 with 3 counters\n- Badgermole Cub 2/2 (summoning sickness)\n- Breeding Pool (p6) 1/1 creature land (tapped)\n\n4 damage would kill Badgermole Cub (2/2) or Breeding Pool (1/1). It would also kill my Gene Pollinators if they have damage marked (but they have 7/8 and 4/5 toughness).\n\nActually, Combustion Technique is probably targeting my Badgermole Cub (2/2) since that's the newest threat. I should counter it with Spider-Sense. But I can also counter the Accumulate Wisdom to prevent card draw. Which is more important?\n\nOpponent has 1 card in hand. Accumulate Wisdom would draw at least 1 card (maybe 3 if they have 3+ Lesson cards in graveyard - they have 2 Lesson cards currently). Combustion Technique kills a creature and exiles it. Saving my creature is probably better, especially since Badgermole Cub provides mana ability when I tap creatures for mana (adds extra G).\n\nI'll counter Combustion Technique.\n\n",
