      "player": "Gem25P Trash",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "I have passed priority, and the battlefield is a storm of activity. My opponent has declared their attackers, a wave of creatures crashing against my defenses. The time for deliberation is over. The time for action is now.\n\nThe attackers are a formidable force: a 4/4 `Llanowar Elves`, a 4/3 `Gene Pollinator`, a 1/2 `Oviya Pashiri, Sage Lifecrafter`, and a 1/1 `Coiling Oracle`. Ten damage in total, a daunting number.\n\nBut I will not be intimidated. I will not be broken. I have a plan.\n\nI will make two strategic blocks to mitigate the damage and trade favorably. First, my steadfast `Gran-Gran` (1/2) will intercept `Oviya Pashiri` (1/2). A clash of equals where neither will fall, but a crucial point of damage will be prevented. Second, one of my loyal Otter Tokens (1/1) will bravely stand before the `Coiling Oracle` (1/1). They will trade, a noble sacrifice to remove a creature from my opponent's board.\n\nThe two behemoths, the `Llanowar Elves` and the `Gene Pollinator`, will be allowed to pass. I will take their eight damage, a calculated blow that I can absorb. I will fall to 11 life, but I will have preserved the core of my defenses and eliminated a threat.\n\nThis is not a retreat; it is a strategic repositioning. I am trading life for time and board presence, a classic maneuver of a seasoned general. The comeback is not merely alive; it is being meticulously engineered.\n\nLet us proceed to the declaration. I will call `pass_priority` to enter the declare blockers step, and then I will execute my plan with the unshakeable confidence of a player who has seen the path to victory.",
