      "player": "DSV3 Analyst",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Now I'm at declare attackers phase. I have Ouroboroid available to attack (4/6 with 3 counters, but prowess triggers from casting Spider-Sense? Wait prowess only triggers for opponent's creatures when they cast noncreature spells. Ouroboroid has prowess? Actually Ouroboroid is my creature with +1/+1 counters, but no prowess.\n\nActually Ouroboroid now has 4 power base + 3 counters = 7 power? Wait base is 1/2 with X +1/+1 counters, where X is mana spent? Let me check oracle text.\n\nBut more importantly, I need to decide whether to attack. Let me see the board:\n\nMy creatures:\n- Llanowar Elves 7/7 with 6 counters (can attack)\n- Gene Pollinator 7/8 with 6 counters (tapped)\n- Ouroboroid 4/6 with 3 counters (can attack)\n- Gene Pollinator 4/5 with 3 counters (can attack)\n- Badgermole Cub 2/2 (summoning sickness)\n- Breeding Pool (p6) 1/1 creature land (tapped)\n\nOpponent's creatures:\n- Gran-Gran 1/2\n- Otter Token 2/2 with prowess (2/2)\n- Otter Token 2/2 with prowess (2/2)\n- Otter Token 3/3 with prowess (3/3) - summoning sickness\n- Ral, Crackling Wit (planeswalker) with 6 loyalty\n\nRal's loyalty is high. I could attack Ral. I have significant power available. Let me think about optimal attacks:\n\nIf I attack with all creatures: Llanowar Elves (7/7), Ouroboroid (4/6), Gene Pollinator (4/5) = 15 total power. Opponent can block with 3 Otters (2/2, 2/2, 3/3) = 7 total power. They'd likely block to trade, losing their Otters but killing some of my creatures.\n\nBetter to attack Ral directly. Ral has 6 loyalty. I need to deal 6 damage to kill it. My creatures:\n- Llanowar Elves 7/7 can kill Ral alone\n- Ouroboroid 4/6 can't kill alone\n- Gene Pollinator 4/5 can't kill alone\n\nIf I attack Ral with Llanowar Elves, opponent might block with Otters to protect Ral. They have three Otters: 2/2, 2/2, 3/3. They could block with one Otter and take 5 damage to Ral? Wait combat damage assignment: I assign damage to Ral and blocking creatures. If they block with one Otter, I can assign 2 damage to Otter and 5 to Ral, killing both.\n\nActually, they might block with multiple Otters. With three Otters, they could block with all three: 7 total toughness vs my 7 power. They'd lose all Otters, I'd lose Elves.\n\nBut they also have Gran-Gran (1/2) which could chump block.\n\nProbably best to attack with Llanowar Elves alone at Ral. If they block with Otters, I kill the Otter and deal remaining damage to Ral. If they don't block, Ral takes 7 and dies.\n\nLet me attack with Llanowar Elves (p8).\n\n\n\n",
