      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Now I have 6 untapped lands (including the new Forest). I can play Keen-Eyed Curator for GG - it's a 3/3 with \"When this creature enters, you may search your library for a Lesson card, reveal it, and put it into your hand.\"\n\nOr Badgermole Cub for 1G - 2/2 with earthbend 1 (make a land into a creature with +1/+1 counter).\n\nOr Mockingbird for XU - 1/1 with flying, prowess, and \"When this creature enters, if X is 3 or greater, draw a card.\"\n\nI have 6 lands available. What's the best play? \n\nKeen-Eyed Curator would let me search for a Lesson card. I have 2 Lesson cards in my graveyard already (maybe from earlier). Lessons are usually instants/sorceries with Learn mechanic. I could get something useful.\n\nBadgermole Cub gives me another earthbend creature, making another land into a creature with +1/+1 counter. My Breeding Pool (p6) is already a creature land with 5 counters. I could target another land like Botanical Sanctum or the new Forest.\n\nMockingbird with X=3 or more (UUU) would draw a card when it enters. I have enough blue sources: Breeding Pool (p22), Multiversal Passage (p5), Botanical Sanctum (p4) can produce blue. That's 3 blue sources. I could cast Mockingbird with X=3 for 4UU total (6 mana) to draw a card and get a 4/4 flying prowess creature? Wait Mockingbird is 1/1 base with X +1/+1 counters. With X=3, it's a 4/4 flying prowess for 4UU.\n\nActually, let me think about mana: I have 2 Breeding Pools (UG), Botanical Sanctum (WU but can produce U), Multiversal Passage (any color), Forest (G), and another Forest (G). So I have UU available easily.\n\nBut Keen-Eyed Curator seems good for card advantage. I'll play that first.\n\n\n\n<functioninvoke name=\"choose_action\">\n<parameter name=\"id\" string=\"true\">p30</parameterinvoke>\n</function_calls>",
